{
  "_note": "Every sound in the game, rendered by the core (crates/core/src/sound/) from these recipes into WAV bytes the page plays; there are no audio files. Frequencies in Hz, times in ms, gains 0 to 1 (the layers sounding at once add up, so keep their sum under about 1), filter Q as WebAudio's, cents as a musician's. master is the 16-bit level of a full-scale sound at 100% volume (Ape Race's corrected level). Write every sound out to listen to with python3 scripts/sounds.py.",
  "_layers": "A layer: wave (sine, square, sawtooth, triangle or noise), freq and an optional to_freq it glides to over the layer (glide exp or linear), at_ms (when it starts), attack_ms, hold_ms, release_ms, fall (curved or linear), gain, an optional filter {type lowpass/highpass/bandpass, freq, to_freq, q}, an optional wobble {rate, cents}, notes [[at_ms, freq], ...] (one copy per note: a tune, or a chord when the times match), repeat {times, every_ms}, and scatter {times, over_ms, cents} (copies strewn by the seed). Noise has no freq; colour it with a filter.",
  "_cues": "A cue: id, layers, an optional vary_cents (the seed moves its whole pitch up to this far either way, so a sound heard again and again is never quite the same), and loop_ms for a loop (everything wraps round; a whole noise layer fills it end to end).",
  "sample_rate": 32000,
  "master": 13000,
  "cues": [
